To draw a chessboard with the given FEN (Forsyth–Edwards Notation) notation in LaTeX, follow these steps:

1. Load necessary packages: Include the following packages in your LaTeX document to generate the chessboard:
   - `skak`: This package provides specialized chessboard environments and symbols.
   - `xfp`: This package is used for precise arithmetic calculations, which will help in laying out the board.

2. Define chessboard dimensions and board coordinates: Declare a few variables to store the dimensions and coordinates of the chessboard as follows:

   ```latex
   \documentclass[12pt]{article}
   \usepackage{skak}
   \usepackage{xfp}

   % Board dimensions
   \newcommand{\BoardWidth}{9.5cm}
   \newcommand{\BoardHeight}{9.5cm}

   % Coordinate system (origin at bottom-left)
   \newcommand{\CellXmargin}{0.18cm} % Margin to left and right
   \newcommand{\CellYmargin}{0.15cm} % Margin to top and bottom
   \newcommand{\CellWidth}{\fpeval{\BoardWidth - 2*\CellXmargin / 8}}
   \newcommand{\CellHeight}{\fpeval{\BoardHeight - 2*\CellYmargin / 8}}
   \newcommand{\CellOriginX}{\fpeval{\CellXmargin + \CellWidth / 16}}
   \newcommand{\CellOriginY}{\fpeval{\CellYmargin + \CellHeight / 16}}
   ```

3. Generate the board using the `chessboard` environment and FEN notation:

   ```latex
   \begin{document}
   \pagestyle{empty}

   \begin{chessboard}[width=\BoardWidth,height=\BoardHeight]
     <FEN>
   \end{chessboard}
   ```

