A binary search algorithm is an efficient method to search for a specific element in a sorted array by comparing the element to be searched with the middle element of the array. The algorithm repeatedly executes the comparison, adjusting the search interval based on the result, until the element is found or the search interval becomes empty. Here is the implementation of a binary search algorithm in C++:

